This document is the contract for where code goes. The definition-of-done gate enforces
the *test* half of it; reviewers enforce the rest.

{% if architecture == 'service-based' -%}
## Service-based

Organise by **service capability**, each with an explicit contract at its edge.

{% if language_stack == 'py-fastapi' -%}
```
src/{{ pkg }}/
  main.py              # composition root — wires services to the API
  health.py            # a capability's logic (pure, unit-testable)
  services/            # one module per service capability
  contracts/           # request/response models (pydantic) — the service boundary
tests/unit/            # capability logic in isolation
tests/integration/     # the app over HTTP (TestClient)
```
{%- elif language_stack == 'ts-node' -%}
```
src/
  index.ts             # composition root
  services/            # one module per service capability
  contracts/           # zod/DTO types — the service boundary
tests/integration/     # service over its transport
# unit tests colocated as *.test.ts next to the code
```
{%- else -%}
```
app/                   # routes / server components
src/services/          # service capabilities
src/contracts/         # DTOs — the service boundary
__tests__/             # unit/component
e2e/                   # end-to-end (Playwright)
```
{%- endif %}

**Rules:** a service never reaches into another service's internals — only its contract.
Business logic is independent of the transport (HTTP) so it is unit-testable without it.
{%- else -%}
## Clean / layered

Dependencies point **inward**: outer layers depend on inner, never the reverse.

{% if language_stack == 'py-fastapi' -%}
```
src/{{ pkg }}/
  domain/              # entities + rules — no framework imports
  application/         # use cases — orchestrates the domain
  adapters/            # FastAPI routes, DB, external I/O
  main.py              # composition root — wires adapters to use cases
tests/unit/            # domain + application, no I/O
tests/integration/     # adapters + the wired app
```
{%- elif language_stack == 'ts-node' -%}
```
src/
  domain/              # entities + rules — no framework imports
  application/         # use cases
  adapters/            # transport, persistence, external I/O
  index.ts             # composition root
tests/integration/     # adapters + wired app
# unit tests colocated as *.test.ts
```
{%- else -%}
```
src/domain/            # entities + rules
src/application/       # use cases
app/                   # Next.js routes = adapters
__tests__/             # unit/component
e2e/                   # end-to-end (Playwright)
```
{%- endif %}

**Rules:** the domain imports nothing from outer layers or frameworks. The web framework
is an adapter, swappable without touching domain or application code.
{%- endif %}

